Rounder Privacy Policy
Last updated: [7-11-2026] · Website: rounder-sa.com · Contact: rounder-sa@gmail.com
1. Who We Are
Rounder ("we", "us") is a home and business services platform in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia. It lets individuals and businesses book services such as maintenance, cleaning, and pest control, 
and connects them with service providers and technicians. 
2. Data We Collect
A. Data you provide
• Account data: name, mobile number, email address, password or verification code.
• Order data: service type, city, address and location details, chosen appointment, notes and photos you attach.
• Business account data: business name, branches and sites, contact persons.
• Service provider and technician data: name, specialty, city, contact details.
• Your communications with customer support.
B. Data collected automatically
• Device and usage data: device type, operating system, device identifiers, crash and performance logs, screens and pages viewed.
• Precise or approximate location (optional, requires your permission in device settings) to set the service address.
• Push notification token if you enable notifications.
C. Payment data (if applicable)
Electronic payments are processed by a licensed payment provider . We do not store your full card details on our servers.
3. How We Use Your Data
• Create, manage, and verify your account.
• Receive orders, schedule appointments, and assign suitable service providers.
• Contact you about your order, confirm appointments, and send updates.
• Improve the app and services, analyze performance, and fix errors.
• Prevent fraud and protect the security of the platform and users.
• Comply with applicable laws in the Kingdom.
• Send marketing offers and alerts .
4. Sharing Your Data
We do not sell your personal data. We share it only as follows:
• Service providers and technicians: the minimum necessary to fulfill your order (name, contact number, address, service details).
• Technical vendors: hosting, cloud storage, notifications, analytics, and SMS, such as [Firebase / Google Analytics / hosting provider], who process data on our behalf and under our instructions.
• Payment providers when electronic payment is used.
• Authorities where required by law or court order.
• Business transfers: in a merger or acquisition, with notice of any material change.
5. Data Retention
We keep your data while your account is active and as long as needed for the purposes above or for legal and accounting obligations, then delete or anonymize it.
6. Data Security
We apply appropriate technical and organizational measures, including encryption in transit and restricted access controls. However, no method of transmission or storage is 100% secure.
7. Your Rights
Under the Saudi Personal Data Protection Law (PDPL) and its regulations, you have the right to:
• Know what data we collect and how we use it.
• Request a copy of your data, or its correction or update.
• Request destruction of your data.
• Withdraw your consent at any time.
• Lodge a complaint with the competent authority.
